Package: tsfm
Title: Native Time-Series Foundation Models for R
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Pedro", "Botz", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An inference engine under development for running open
    time-series foundation models natively in R. It provides a
    'from_pretrained()'-style loader with an open architecture registry, a
    versioned execution contract and conformance harness, explicit capability
    metadata, batched panel inference with device resolution, and a standard
    forecast object backed by 'distributional'. The first supported native
    architecture is TimesFM 2.5, loaded from an immutable checkpoint and
    verified against pinned reference outputs. The engine is
    framework-neutral, with optional adapters for 'tidymodels' (via 'hardhat'
    and 'parsnip') and the tidyverts (via 'fabletools').
